                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4f31075a-1f91-3a41-b19c-8ed7bfa4ec40",
                        "entry_id": "4156e532-baa4-3c3c-9be5-bff22f528953",
                        "glosses": [
                            "für Hund"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "derogatory"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b925ea7-7fe2-4c1a-955e-a079e94df1e5",
                                "sense_id": "4f31075a-1f91-3a41-b19c-8ed7bfa4ec40",
                                "text": "Was will denn die Töle hier im Zimmer?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e15fc015-85d4-4e1a-a076-91830ac8bea8",
                                "sense_id": "4f31075a-1f91-3a41-b19c-8ed7bfa4ec40",
                                "text": "Das Schlimmste, was man uns antun konnte, war, wenn einer unseren kleinen Freund als Töle oder Köter bezeichnete."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "846248bf-11c8-46a1-81f2-9cece6f06153",
                                "sense_id": "4f31075a-1f91-3a41-b19c-8ed7bfa4ec40",
                                "text": "„Ich überlege, ob ich mir eine dieser Hochfrequenzpfeifen kaufe, eine Hundepfeife, und damit jedes Stockwerk ablaufe, um rauszufinden, hinter welcher Tür die Töle nervt.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e581c23-6a23-4be9-b4d9-8dd4afee8a05",
                                "sense_id": "4f31075a-1f91-3a41-b19c-8ed7bfa4ec40",
                                "text": "„Was hatten wir mit dieser Frau und ihrer jaulenden Töle zu schaffen?“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6224ed52-bdf9-4fd0-8a5b-d0b984119699",
                        "source_entry_id": "4156e532-baa4-3c3c-9be5-bff22f528953",
                        "source_sense_id": "4f31075a-1f91-3a41-b19c-8ed7bfa4ec40",
                        "source_sense_description": "abwertend: für Hund",
                        "target_lang_word": "cur",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cur",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f456aaab-9e66-3b15-be61-2abe9e6a36c6",
                                        "entry_id": "853e333d-f80a-321a-9f19-ee0bfe8ceabd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A contemptible or inferior dog."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "humorous"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1627a352-3ea8-40c0-861d-a327919022af",
                                                "sense_id": "f456aaab-9e66-3b15-be61-2abe9e6a36c6",
                                                "text": "A fals double tunge is more fiers and fell\nThen Cerberus the cur couching in the kenel of hel;\nWherof hereafter, I thinke for to write,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23a187af-6e9a-490f-a6a2-fe02a51104d2",
                                                "sense_id": "f456aaab-9e66-3b15-be61-2abe9e6a36c6",
                                                "text": "you have many enemies, that know not why they are so, but, like to village-curs, bark when their fellows do."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "871bec4f-daaa-4ac1-9984-31efbc7c915a",
                                                "sense_id": "f456aaab-9e66-3b15-be61-2abe9e6a36c6",
                                                "text": "A Churliſh Envious Curr vvas gotten into a Manger, and there lay Growling and Snarling to keep the Horſes from their Provender. The Dog Eat None himſelf, and yet rather Ventur'd the Starving his Own Carcaſe then he would ſuffer any thing elfe to be the Better for't."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b219a2cc-84a5-467a-be4e-8fd9fbb24c14",
                                                "sense_id": "f456aaab-9e66-3b15-be61-2abe9e6a36c6",
                                                "text": "He threw the soapsuds skilfully over a wretched little yellow cur he had, then turning his face to the agent's house, he shouted from the distance, \"All the men gone last night!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b54401a1-5bea-4853-810a-04865a800e92",
                                                "sense_id": "f456aaab-9e66-3b15-be61-2abe9e6a36c6",
                                                "text": "\"You have no more spirit than a mongrel cur. You lie down on the ground and ask people to trample on you.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4696ee56-7c28-3337-83e1-c6cb811dc9f2",
                                        "entry_id": "853e333d-f80a-321a-9f19-ee0bfe8ceabd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A detestable person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "humorous"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9210cac8-9ee4-499e-bc7b-1b9419abb2dc",
                                                "sense_id": "4696ee56-7c28-3337-83e1-c6cb811dc9f2",
                                                "text": "This butcher's cur is venom-mouth'd, and I have not the power to muzzle him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae1f8b5b-113f-4695-99f5-f084ed38a109",
                                                "sense_id": "4696ee56-7c28-3337-83e1-c6cb811dc9f2",
                                                "text": "\"Who 's a cur - now - hey?\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ba05934-d98b-4f53-9fd4-00a5269ff6c4",
                                                "sense_id": "4696ee56-7c28-3337-83e1-c6cb811dc9f2",
                                                "text": "Clayton interrupted him. “Stop!” he cried. “Stop! What manner of cur are you that you traduce the character of a good woman whom we believe dead! God!”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2e3814bd-db84-30f5-80b9-76548bae868e",
                                        "entry_id": "853e333d-f80a-321a-9f19-ee0bfe8ceabd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sheepdog or watchdog."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fff97f7-d2fe-4645-8743-8f4214e33bd9",
                                                "sense_id": "2e3814bd-db84-30f5-80b9-76548bae868e",
                                                "text": "Then send our Curs to gather up the Sheep"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "552f6622-fea0-4394-9ac3-a71fe82a9b57",
                                                "sense_id": "2e3814bd-db84-30f5-80b9-76548bae868e",
                                                "text": "\"He's a good sharp cur,\" or \"a good cur,\" is said of any dog that barks at strangers and guards his master's property."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "031ed9af-75dd-4806-9046-f69948f3144e",
                        "source_entry_id": "4156e532-baa4-3c3c-9be5-bff22f528953",
                        "source_sense_id": "4f31075a-1f91-3a41-b19c-8ed7bfa4ec40",
                        "source_sense_description": "abwertend: für Hund",
                        "target_lang_word": "clebs",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "clebs",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "917345d7-75fa-3b28-ac9b-f28c133a7f1d",
                                        "entry_id": "54c7c321-04ac-340b-b7ef-8b994b861f2c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chien."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "familiar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4de80203-eacc-4846-bc87-05acbe1c7d27",
                                                "sense_id": "917345d7-75fa-3b28-ac9b-f28c133a7f1d",
                                                "text": "Ton clebs a encore fait ses besoins devant la porte !"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0060451e-296e-4e5c-8ee7-da9b6997077c",
                                                "sense_id": "917345d7-75fa-3b28-ac9b-f28c133a7f1d",
                                                "text": "Il le regarde s’éloigner dans la lumière crue de l’avenue, avec son affreux clebs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d6fc29b-a406-4cdc-9898-d125bb44b130",
                                                "sense_id": "917345d7-75fa-3b28-ac9b-f28c133a7f1d",
                                                "text": "Je ne pense pas que Dingo était un dingo australien, mais tout bonnement un clebs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94bae66c-d352-4ee4-91ee-d2b5104401ef",
                                                "sense_id": "917345d7-75fa-3b28-ac9b-f28c133a7f1d",
                                                "text": "Toute la meute dévale, fonce zigzag, les clebs lui râlent, coursent au train."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e20e865-17f9-48b0-a76b-f887ca75da7e",
                                                "sense_id": "917345d7-75fa-3b28-ac9b-f28c133a7f1d",
                                                "text": "Tout plutôt que de le faire piquer. Il ne tuerait pas ce clebs, c’était dit."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bb97633c-c38d-4fe3-a859-e304e5db9f18",
                        "source_entry_id": "4156e532-baa4-3c3c-9be5-bff22f528953",
                        "source_sense_id": "4f31075a-1f91-3a41-b19c-8ed7bfa4ec40",
                        "source_sense_description": "abwertend: für Hund",
                        "target_lang_word": "clébard",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "clébard",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bae4b3dd-b311-33b1-b197-eb313e23843a",
                                        "entry_id": "9db5551b-58d5-3743-af71-7e0755b9f336",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chien."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a03376c1-ee3c-4b86-b97d-9c7460c8275e",
                                                "sense_id": "bae4b3dd-b311-33b1-b197-eb313e23843a",
                                                "text": "Faute de mieux, Marçais a suivi sa mère comme son ombre, avec le maigre espoir qu’elle retrouve son fils : la promenade du clébard, un horrible cocker court sur pattes, les courses au Codec voisin, et même la virée en bus dans l’après-midi, jusqu’au Prisunic des Champs-Élysées, où elle a acheté tout un tas de produits de beauté."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f662879f-3ecd-4323-80de-d089ff781dab",
                                                "sense_id": "bae4b3dd-b311-33b1-b197-eb313e23843a",
                                                "text": "Un mur de pierres blanches jointées en losange protégeait cette portion de trottoir des regards et servait de crottoir aux clébards du quartier."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6aefb5d5-086a-4a81-b92f-d2d0646c67b4",
                                                "sense_id": "bae4b3dd-b311-33b1-b197-eb313e23843a",
                                                "text": "Je n’ai que de la haine à lui donner : brûlures, escarres, claques et claques et claques encore, coups de fouet, coups de latte. Mon rêve le plus fou ? Faire de lui un chien. Un clébard ! Ouah ! Ouah !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "41264dda-40c3-4b01-aa07-311eafb9c621",
                        "source_entry_id": "4156e532-baa4-3c3c-9be5-bff22f528953",
